1
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,270
What was she like?

2
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:31,330
She,

3
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:36,230
she had red hair.

4
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,900
-How big were her feet?  -What do you want me to say?

5
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:46,040
I want you to tell me what it was like to have someone.

6
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:48,120
To be with someone.

7
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,790
To love someone and have them love you back.

8
00:02:54,130 --> 00:02:57,870
We're all gonna die a lot sooner than I'd planned.

9
00:02:58,730 --> 00:03:01,030
You're the closest I'll ever get to knowing.

10
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:06,040
So you and Gilly never?

11
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,120
No.

12
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:09,030
She just had a baby.

13
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,990
And she never offered.

14
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:15,840
But if she had,

15
00:03:17,390 --> 00:03:18,520
you would have?

16
00:03:19,670 --> 00:03:21,500
You'd have broken your vows?

17
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,910
The interesting thing is,

18
00:03:28,630 --> 00:03:31,300
our vows never specifically forbid

19
00:03:31,310 --> 00:03:33,140
intimate relations with women.

20
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:34,530
What?

21
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,760
"I shall take no wife," Yes,

22
00:03:36,760 --> 00:03:38,150
that's in there. There's no denying that.

23
00:03:38,150 --> 00:03:40,940
"I shall father no children." It's very specific.

24
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:43,660
But what do our vows have to say about other

25
00:03:43,710 --> 00:03:47,000
activities is open to interpretation.

26
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:52,080
I don't think Ser Alliser cares much for interpretation.

27
00:03:56,410 --> 00:03:59,690
Anyway, there's nothing for him to interpret.

28
00:04:00,030 --> 00:04:01,120
We didn't.

29
00:04:05,230 --> 00:04:06,710
So what's it like?

30
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:10,430
It's,

31
00:04:11,700 --> 00:04:15,310
there's this person, this whole other person.

32
00:04:16,230 --> 00:04:19,000
And you're wrapped up in them and they're wrapped up in you.

33
00:04:19,930 --> 00:04:21,030
And you,

34
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:22,970
for a little,

35
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,630
for a little while, you're more than just you.

36
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:28,970
You're, I don't know. I'm not a bleeding poet.

37
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:30,550
No, you're really not.

38
00:04:31,370 --> 00:04:32,900
What did I get for it?

39
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:35,270
An arrow six inches from my heart.

40
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:39,690
There'll be arrows for all of us soon, I imagine.

41
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,350
There will.

42
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:44,690
They've already done the worst thing to me they could ever do.

43
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:49,390
Go get some sleep, Sam.

44
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,760
I'll take this watch.

45
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:36,910
Did I ever tell you about her?

46
00:05:37,730 --> 00:05:41,080
-My Sheila?  -Yes.

47
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:43,440
That was a night to remember.

48
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:46,950
Of course, I'd had a good bit to drink.

49
00:05:47,790 --> 00:05:49,240
Her fangs were sharp,

50
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:52,180
but she knew how to use them.

51
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:56,030
And she was nice and soft down below.

52
00:05:56,030 --> 00:05:58,920
No, she was no ordinary beast.

53
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,240
Many is the man who.

54
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,780
I know you never fucked a bear.

55
00:06:02,850 --> 00:06:05,260
You know you never fucked a bear.

56
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:08,840
Right now I don't want to think about the bear you never fucked.

57
00:06:08,940 --> 00:06:11,780
Right now all I want to think about

58
00:06:11,780 --> 00:06:15,220
is each one of these arrows finding its way into a crow's heart.

59
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:18,150
We could be waiting here a while.

60
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:19,260
Good.

61
00:06:19,430 --> 00:06:21,910
The longer we wait, the more arrows I'll have.

62
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:29,490
They came up here to our land

63
00:06:29,490 --> 00:06:31,980
and put up a big wall and said it was theirs.

64
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:34,030
Then they started hunting us down.

65
00:06:36,230 --> 00:06:39,620
This time, we're the ones doing the hunting.

66
00:06:41,070 --> 00:06:43,340
You've got a lot to say about killing.

67
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:46,280
Even more words than arrows.

68
00:06:47,290 --> 00:06:50,780
Back in those villages, I killed just as many of them as you did.

69
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:52,920
More, I reckon.

70
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:57,000
Yes, but none of those were your crow lover.

71
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,720
I probably killed him already.

72
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,190
So you've said.

73
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,540
And if not,

74
00:07:02,490 --> 00:07:04,120
the only thing left of him

75
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,360
is gonna be his fun bits hanging around my neck.

76
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:07,860
More words.

77
00:07:07,970 --> 00:07:10,440
Know what I think you do when you see him?

78
00:07:10,610 --> 00:07:14,750
Serve him up a nice juicy slice of ginger minge.

79
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:20,480
You been thinking about that ginger minge?

80
00:07:22,330 --> 00:07:24,450
Wondering what it tasts like.

81
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:28,260
Maybe I have.

82
00:07:29,690 --> 00:07:32,030
Jon Snow is mine.

83
00:07:33,370 --> 00:07:35,800
Anyone else tries to kill him,

84
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:37,860
I'll have an arrow for them.

85
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:45,200
And not one of your bald friends is fast enough to stop me.

86
00:08:06,390 --> 00:08:10,940
And what is it that couldn't wait until morning, Tarly?

87
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:12,330
Maester Aemon.

88
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:15,750
-How did you know?  -That it was you?

89
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:18,290
Who else but Samwell Tarly

90
00:08:18,290 --> 00:08:20,110
would be wasting candles

91
00:08:20,110 --> 00:08:22,820
to read in the middle of the night?

92
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:29,020
-Let me help you.  -Oh, no need.

93
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:32,410
I know my way around this library

94
00:08:32,410 --> 00:08:35,290
better than any other place in Castle Black.

95
00:08:35,570 --> 00:08:37,400
Thousands of books

96
00:08:37,450 --> 00:08:39,550
and no eyes to read them.

97
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:43,980
Old age is a wonderful source of ironies

98
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,820
if nothing else.

99
00:08:46,450 --> 00:08:48,460
But you didn't answer my question.

100
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,550
What are you reading?

101
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:52,480
Maester Faull.

102
00:08:52,480 --> 00:08:55,670
Ah, the wildlings.

103
00:08:55,670 --> 00:08:59,530
I can assure you that the closest Maester Faull

104
00:08:59,530 --> 00:09:02,870
ever got to a wildling was this very library.

105
00:09:02,870 --> 00:09:05,580
But what he says about what they do,

106
00:09:06,150 --> 00:09:07,680
it's all true.

107
00:09:08,250 --> 00:09:11,030
It's exactly what the survivors of their raids report.

108
00:09:11,030 --> 00:09:15,670
Yes, imagine the stories wildlings tell about us.

109
00:09:17,230 --> 00:09:20,230
Love is the death of duty.

110
00:09:21,150 --> 00:09:24,340
I told that to your friend Jon Snow once.

111
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:28,200
He didn't listen and neither did you.

112
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:32,360
Which is why you've abandoned your watch atop the Wall

113
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:36,210
to come here and read about the terrible things

114
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:40,430
that may have happened to the girl you love.

115
00:09:40,570 --> 00:09:43,400
I don't love her.

116
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:45,030
-Yes, you do.  -No.

117
00:09:45,030 --> 00:09:47,360
Yes, you do.

118
00:09:47,370 --> 00:09:51,040
Heard it in your voice when you first brought her to me.

119
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:53,240
I remember how it sounds.

120
00:09:53,570 --> 00:09:55,610
I was in love once.

121
00:09:55,610 --> 00:09:57,130
You were?

122
00:09:57,720 --> 00:10:01,100
You can imagine all manner of horrors

123
00:10:01,100 --> 00:10:03,850
befalling that poor girl and her child.

124
00:10:03,850 --> 00:10:08,690
Is it so difficult to imagine that an old person was once,

125
00:10:08,690 --> 00:10:10,880
more or less, like you?

126
00:10:11,070 --> 00:10:12,670
I'm sorry, Maester.

127
00:10:13,810 --> 00:10:15,560
I didn't mean it like that.

128
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:18,910
Do you know who I was before I came here?

129
00:10:19,530 --> 00:10:23,200
What I could have been if I'd only said the word?

130
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:26,170
Of course you do.

131
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:30,440
I met many girls when I was Aemon Targaryen.

132
00:10:31,190 --> 00:10:34,090
A future king always does.

133
00:10:35,020 --> 00:10:38,050
Some of them were quite forward

134
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:40,990
in their attempts to win my affections.

135
00:10:41,970 --> 00:10:43,890
One of them succeeded.

136
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,900
I was very young.

137
00:10:48,190 --> 00:10:49,600
Who was she?

138
00:10:51,540 --> 00:10:54,270
I could tell you everything about her.

139
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:56,140
Who she was,

140
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:57,740
how we met,

141
00:10:58,030 --> 00:11:00,040
the color of her eyes,

142
00:11:00,270 --> 00:11:02,600
and the shape of her nose.

143
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,420
I can see her

144
00:11:07,470 --> 00:11:10,000
right in front of me.

145
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:13,820
She's more real than you are.

146
00:11:18,210 --> 00:11:22,490
We could spend all night trading tales of lost loves.

147
00:11:22,690 --> 00:11:25,870
Nothing makes the past a sweeter place to visit

148
00:11:25,870 --> 00:11:28,710
than the prospect of imminent death.

149
00:11:29,470 --> 00:11:31,240
Go to bed, Tarly.

150
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:39,930
Sorry, I can't open the gate for anybody. Orders.

151
00:11:39,930 --> 00:11:42,060
You don't understand. They killed everyone.

152
00:11:42,070 --> 00:11:43,910
Everyone but me and my baby.

153
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:46,520
They're out there. I saw them on my way here.

154
00:11:46,520 --> 00:11:48,980
They may have seen me. They may have followed me. Please.

155
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:49,980
I'm sorry, I can't.

156
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:51,370
If they find us out here, you don't know.

157
00:11:51,370 --> 00:11:53,570
Pyp! Open the gate.

158
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:56,270
-I can't.  -Sam, is that you?

159
00:11:56,270 --> 00:11:57,370
Yes.

160
00:11:57,930 --> 00:12:00,280
Thorne gave me strict orders to not open the gate.

161
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:03,000
Oh, Pyp, open the fucking gate!

162
00:12:04,730 --> 00:12:06,150
I never heard you curse before.

163
00:12:06,150 --> 00:12:08,260
Yes, well, best get used to it.

164
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,850
Are you all right?

165
00:12:18,170 --> 00:12:20,280
Shh, you're all right.

166
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:24,440
Of course you are, my brave little fella.

167
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:27,630
-It was horrible.  -I'm so, so sorry.

168
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:29,200
I didn't know until I got back.

169
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,780
Don't let them send me away, Sam.

170
00:12:30,780 --> 00:12:32,700
-Never.  -I know there's no women allowed.

171
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:35,970
Anyone who tries to throw you out will be having words with me.

172
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:38,970
From now on, wherever you go,

173
00:12:40,130 --> 00:12:41,570
I go, too.

174
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:53,210
Get ready!

175
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:56,020
-Man the gate!  -Ready yourselves!

176
00:12:56,720 --> 00:12:58,000
Make haste!

177
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,940
-Prepare!  -Up on the Wall!

178
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:01,760
Quickly! Up! Up!

179
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:04,690
How many? How many are there?

180
00:13:07,620 --> 00:13:08,960
Beyond the trees!

181
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,550
It's time.

182
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:04,890
Light them up! Light them all!

183
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:14,960
Move!

184
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,800
Pick up the pace!

185
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:21,470
Come on, come on.

186
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:31,090
Here we go, boys, there's one.

187
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:34,260
Let's go. There's two.

188
00:14:37,030 --> 00:14:38,520
Let's get the next load.

189
00:14:42,860 --> 00:14:44,830
That's the last of the oil, Ser Alliser.

190
00:14:46,330 --> 00:14:48,210
100,000 you say?

191
00:14:49,310 --> 00:14:50,310
Yes, Ser.

192
00:14:51,810 --> 00:14:53,620
You can say it if you like.

193
00:14:54,740 --> 00:14:57,410
We should have sealed the tunnel while we had the chance,

194
00:14:57,850 --> 00:14:59,620
like you suggested.

195
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,800
It was a difficult decision either way, Ser.

196
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:09,530
Do you know what leadership means, Lord Snow?

197
00:15:10,530 --> 00:15:12,930
It means that the person in charge gets second-guessed

198
00:15:12,930 --> 00:15:15,450
by every clever little twat with a mouth.

199
00:15:15,950 --> 00:15:18,290
But if he starts second-guessing himself,

200
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,480
that's the end,

201
00:15:20,220 --> 00:15:23,520
for him, for the clever little twats,

202
00:15:24,090 --> 00:15:25,020
for everyone.

203
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,300
This is not the end. Not for us.

204
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:30,180
Not if you lot do your duty

205
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:32,880
for however long it takes to beat them back.

206
00:15:34,850 --> 00:15:37,320
And then you get to go on hating me

207
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:39,150
and I get to go on wishing

208
00:15:39,150 --> 00:15:41,590
your wildling whore had finished the job.

209
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:06,610
You'll be safe down here.

210
00:16:06,990 --> 00:16:08,750
I'll check on you as soon as I can.

211
00:16:09,930 --> 00:16:11,420
You're leaving me again?

212
00:16:13,030 --> 00:16:14,590
I'm not leaving you.

213
00:16:14,590 --> 00:16:15,450
You're going up there and

214
00:16:15,450 --> 00:16:17,450
we're staying down here. That's leaving.

215
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:19,760
You said from now on we'd stay together.

216
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:22,400
I didn't mean in the same room.

217
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,720
What are you going to do out there?

218
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,370
-Help my brothers.  -How?

219
00:16:26,950 --> 00:16:28,940
You're going to fight the free folk when they come?

220
00:16:28,940 --> 00:16:32,020
They'll kill you. In Mole's Town, they killed everyone.

221
00:16:32,020 --> 00:16:35,580
I can't just hide here with you, while they're fighting out there.

222
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:38,120
Why not? You won't matter up there.

223
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,600
You will down here.

224
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:44,240
I am a man of the Night's Watch, Gilly.

225
00:16:44,870 --> 00:16:46,510
I made a promise to defend the Wall

226
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:48,270
and I have to keep it,

227
00:16:49,090 --> 00:16:50,820
because that's what men do.

228
00:17:03,700 --> 00:17:05,810
Promise me you won't die.

229
00:17:08,930 --> 00:17:12,030
I promise you, I won't die.

230
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:49,420
There's a lot more wildlings on the other side of the Wall than this side.

231
00:17:50,080 --> 00:17:51,970
We've got loads of weapons and things.

232
00:17:52,520 --> 00:17:54,490
It's the perfect place for us to be.

233
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:56,310
I've never thrown a spear before.

234
00:17:56,850 --> 00:17:59,550
I've never held a sword with a proper edge.

235
00:18:00,530 --> 00:18:02,190
This is no place for me to be.

236
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:05,680
You're not afraid?

237
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:08,060
Of course I'm afraid.

238
00:18:08,530 --> 00:18:10,620
There's a band of wildlings coming to kill us.

239
00:18:10,630 --> 00:18:12,210
If you're afraid of a band of wildlings,

240
00:18:12,210 --> 00:18:14,740
how in seven hells did you manage to kill a white walker?

241
00:18:20,910 --> 00:18:23,570
I didn't know I was going to kill it.

242
00:18:24,430 --> 00:18:25,400
But I had to do something.

243
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:26,250
I didn't have any choice.

244
00:18:26,250 --> 00:18:28,460
It was going to kill Gilly and take the baby.

245
00:18:30,550 --> 00:18:33,740
If someone had asked me my name right then,

246
00:18:33,740 --> 00:18:34,960
I wouldn't have known.

247
00:18:37,270 --> 00:18:40,080
I wasn't Samwell Tarly anymore.

248
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:42,760
I wasn't a steward in the Night's Watch

249
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:45,360
or son of Randyll Tarly or any of that.

250
00:18:47,230 --> 00:18:48,480
I was nothing at all.

251
00:18:50,740 --> 00:18:52,150
And when you're nothing at all,

252
00:18:53,560 --> 00:18:55,340
there's no more reason to be afraid.

253
00:18:57,490 --> 00:18:58,860
But you're afraid now?

254
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,240
Yes, well.

255
00:19:03,960 --> 00:19:05,490
I'm not nothing anymore.

256
00:19:25,150 --> 00:19:26,870
Most of their men are up top.

257
00:19:27,040 --> 00:19:29,920
Didn't count more than 20 down here. Leftovers.

258
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:32,070
They got a big fat one and a little bony one manning the front.

259
00:19:32,070 --> 00:19:33,220
How high are the walls?

260
00:19:33,220 --> 00:19:35,740
Well, we'll be up and over before they know what's happened.

261
00:19:38,270 --> 00:19:40,520
Let's kill some crows!

262
00:19:42,110 --> 00:19:43,880
Come on!

263
00:20:01,970 --> 00:20:03,340
Come on, brothers!

264
00:21:18,910 --> 00:21:20,510
Archers, nock.

265
00:21:20,510 --> 00:21:22,270
Everyone else hold.

266
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:24,940
No!

267
00:21:28,290 --> 00:21:31,280
I said nock and hold, you cunts!

268
00:21:31,450 --> 00:21:34,080
-Does nock mean draw?  -No, Ser!

269
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:37,520
-Does fucking hold mean fucking drop?  -No, Ser!

270
00:21:37,520 --> 00:21:40,570
-You all plan to die here tonight?  -No, Ser!

271
00:21:40,580 --> 00:21:43,520
That's very good to hear. Draw!

272
00:21:47,570 --> 00:21:49,690
No, down below!

273
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:01,500
Draw! Light them up.

274
00:22:16,360 --> 00:22:18,890
Come on, get up!

275
00:22:18,950 --> 00:22:20,800
They're attacking the southern gate!

276
00:22:20,970 --> 00:22:22,340
-Now?  -Now.

277
00:22:26,770 --> 00:22:29,760
I'm going down there. Brother Slynt, you have the Wall.

278
00:22:29,760 --> 00:22:30,560
What?

279
00:22:32,620 --> 00:22:35,740
What are you fucking waiting for? Loose!

280
00:22:36,470 --> 00:22:39,160
You heard the man. Loose!

281
00:23:16,490 --> 00:23:17,940
You, over there.

282
00:23:22,640 --> 00:23:24,050
-Did you get one?  -No.

283
00:23:26,520 --> 00:23:28,760
Ah, shit, Pyp! Shit.

284
00:23:28,760 --> 00:23:30,040
-Sam.  -Yeah?

285
00:23:30,150 --> 00:23:31,360
I think we're gonna die.

286
00:23:32,250 --> 00:23:33,880
If you keep missing, we will.

287
00:23:44,210 --> 00:23:45,790
Come on!

288
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:51,670
Brothers!

289
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:56,310
100 generations have defended this castle.

290
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:58,580
She's never fallen before.

291
00:23:58,630 --> 00:24:00,570
She will not fall tonight.

292
00:24:00,710 --> 00:24:03,090
Those are Thenns at our walls.

293
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:06,390
They eat the flesh of the men they kill.

294
00:24:06,660 --> 00:24:09,130
Do you want to fill the belly of a Thenn tonight?

295
00:24:09,130 --> 00:24:10,120
No!

296
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:12,020
Tonight, we fight.

297
00:24:12,020 --> 00:24:14,450
And when the sun rises, I promise you,

298
00:24:14,450 --> 00:24:16,730
Castle Black will stand!

299
00:24:17,520 --> 00:24:20,060
The Night's Watch will stand.

300
00:24:22,690 --> 00:24:26,390
With me now! Now with me!

301
00:25:22,580 --> 00:25:25,200
No discipline. No training.

302
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:28,010
Gang of thieves, that's all this is.

303
00:25:28,370 --> 00:25:30,740
I commanded the City Watch of King's Landing.

304
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:32,590
Those men obeyed orders.

305
00:25:32,590 --> 00:25:34,600
We can't just let them attack the gate.

306
00:25:34,600 --> 00:25:37,980
The bars of those gates are four inches of cold-rolled steel.

307
00:25:37,980 --> 00:25:40,520
Those are giants riding mammoths down there!

308
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:42,980
Do you think your cold-rolled steel is gonna stop them?

309
00:25:42,980 --> 00:25:44,430
No such thing as giants.

310
00:25:45,170 --> 00:25:46,680
A story for the children.

311
00:25:48,950 --> 00:25:50,010
Brother Slynt.

312
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:53,100
We just got word that Ser Alliser needs you below.

313
00:25:55,870 --> 00:25:58,430
You're the most experienced man he's got, Ser, and he needs you.

314
00:25:59,660 --> 00:26:00,790
Needed below?

315
00:26:01,400 --> 00:26:02,860
Yes. Yes.

316
00:26:12,900 --> 00:26:16,020
Archers, nock your arrows!

317
00:26:16,370 --> 00:26:18,020
Nock arrows!

318
00:26:18,800 --> 00:26:20,270
Draw!

319
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,840
Loose!

320
00:26:38,220 --> 00:26:40,120
They won't summit before dawn.

321
00:26:40,230 --> 00:26:41,140
How do you know that?

322
00:26:41,600 --> 00:26:43,510
Because I've made that climb.

323
00:26:43,510 --> 00:26:45,920
I think they're in a bigger hurry than you were.

324
00:26:50,010 --> 00:26:51,180
Hold the bridge!

325
00:26:51,560 --> 00:26:53,280
Hold, wait for it!

326
00:26:54,520 --> 00:26:56,110
Come on with the rocks!

327
00:27:02,320 --> 00:27:03,200
Nock!

328
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:06,380
Draw!

329
00:27:10,150 --> 00:27:11,670
Loose!

330
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:31,940
Down!

331
00:28:07,750 --> 00:28:09,440
No! No!

332
00:28:28,460 --> 00:28:30,060
To the gate. Come on, let's move.

333
00:28:33,790 --> 00:28:34,790
It's gonna open.

334
00:29:40,040 --> 00:29:42,210
I got one right through the heart. He's dead.

335
00:29:42,210 --> 00:29:44,740
-Oh, is it over?  -No.

336
00:29:44,840 --> 00:29:45,940
Well, then.

337
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:56,920
You're all right. You're all right.

338
00:29:59,730 --> 00:30:00,550
I'll get help.

339
00:30:04,280 --> 00:30:05,660
Maester Aemon is coming.

340
00:30:06,220 --> 00:30:07,670
He's gonna make it all right.

341
00:30:19,660 --> 00:30:21,640
-Now.  -Now!

342
00:31:55,060 --> 00:31:56,450
The outer gate won't hold.

343
00:31:57,150 --> 00:31:59,500
Take five men, hold the inner gate.

344
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:00,370
Aye.

345
00:32:03,940 --> 00:32:04,970
Hold the gate.

346
00:32:06,130 --> 00:32:07,430
If they make it through.

347
00:32:10,340 --> 00:32:11,390
They won't.

348
00:32:14,210 --> 00:32:16,630
Come on, Hill. And you, Cooper.

349
00:32:17,250 --> 00:32:18,810
You three, on me.

350
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,650
Come on, you lazy bastards.

351
00:32:26,210 --> 00:32:27,050
Oil.

352
00:32:29,410 --> 00:32:30,790
Oil on the ramp!

353
00:32:40,530 --> 00:32:41,850
Protect the gate!

354
00:33:16,240 --> 00:33:17,360
Get him inside.

355
00:33:21,530 --> 00:33:23,740
Hold the fucking gate!

356
00:33:23,860 --> 00:33:24,990
Hold it!

357
00:34:24,290 --> 00:34:25,760
We need more men down here.

358
00:34:25,760 --> 00:34:28,220
-We have to hold the gate.  -But we need men here.

359
00:34:28,230 --> 00:34:30,530
Tell Jon. He's in command.

360
00:34:30,800 --> 00:34:31,910
Let's go.

361
00:34:41,210 --> 00:34:43,490
Get me to the top! You hear me?!

362
00:34:48,810 --> 00:34:50,640
Your name's Olly, right?

363
00:34:51,410 --> 00:34:54,030
Listen to me, Olly. Get me to the top.

364
00:34:54,640 --> 00:34:57,180
And when we give the signal, bring us back down.

365
00:34:58,430 --> 00:34:59,300
You hear me?

366
00:35:04,520 --> 00:35:07,030
Find a weapon, Olly. Fight them.

367
00:35:39,630 --> 00:35:42,000
Clear the way! Let's go!

368
00:35:42,080 --> 00:35:44,170
-Out of the way!  -Get out of here!

369
00:36:01,840 --> 00:36:03,060
Cut the rope!

370
00:36:10,200 --> 00:36:11,540
-Wait!  -No!

371
00:36:27,170 --> 00:36:28,970
-We need more archers.  -Here I am.

372
00:36:29,050 --> 00:36:31,070
-Come on.  -Quickly.

373
00:36:33,790 --> 00:36:35,260
What are you doing up here?

374
00:36:35,930 --> 00:36:37,730
The wildlings are over the walls.

375
00:36:38,180 --> 00:36:39,750
Ser Alliser's fallen.

376
00:36:40,060 --> 00:36:42,040
The castle won't stand much longer.

377
00:36:44,120 --> 00:36:47,170
Edd, you have the Wall.

378
00:36:49,590 --> 00:36:52,030
If they try the mammoths again, drop fire on them.

379
00:36:52,090 --> 00:36:54,660
If the climbers get too high, drop the scythe on them.

380
00:37:00,430 --> 00:37:02,610
Come, brothers. Now fight with me!

381
00:37:03,700 --> 00:37:06,660
Might as well enjoy our last night, right, boys?

382
00:37:07,280 --> 00:37:09,490
Light the fuckers up!

383
00:37:09,760 --> 00:37:12,400
Nock! Draw!

384
00:37:13,260 --> 00:37:15,110
Loose!

385
00:37:24,240 --> 00:37:25,220
How are we gonna stop that?

386
00:37:25,230 --> 00:37:26,860
Shot 20 arrows in him already.

387
00:37:26,870 --> 00:37:28,260
You heard Jon. We hold the gate.

388
00:37:28,260 --> 00:37:29,680
Jon Snow's not Lord Commander.

389
00:37:29,680 --> 00:37:30,950
We hold the gate!

390
00:37:40,250 --> 00:37:42,650
Mother, save me. Father, save me.

391
00:37:42,690 --> 00:37:43,980
The gods aren't down here.

392
00:37:44,020 --> 00:37:45,840
It's the six of us. You hear me?

393
00:37:52,010 --> 00:37:54,340
Night gathers and now my watch begins.

394
00:37:54,570 --> 00:37:56,370
It shall not end until my death.

395
00:37:56,710 --> 00:37:59,200
I shall take no wife, hold no lands,

396
00:37:59,200 --> 00:38:00,660
father no children.

397
00:38:00,840 --> 00:38:03,340
I shall wear no crown and win no glory.

398
00:38:03,340 --> 00:38:05,870
I shall live and die at my post.

399
00:38:05,870 --> 00:38:07,800
I am the sword in the darkness.

400
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:09,650
I am the watcher on the walls.

401
00:38:09,650 --> 00:38:12,670
I am the shield that guards the realms of men.

402
00:38:12,670 --> 00:38:16,260
I pledge my life and honor to the Night's Watch

403
00:38:16,260 --> 00:38:19,290
for this night and all the nights to come!

404
00:38:25,060 --> 00:38:26,590
I don't want you out there.

405
00:38:26,910 --> 00:38:28,590
You can't protect me forever.

406
00:38:28,690 --> 00:38:31,220
There won't be anywhere to hide if the castle falls.

407
00:38:34,630 --> 00:38:36,670
I need him more than I need you.

408
00:39:50,380 --> 00:39:51,370
We need you, boy.

409
00:42:12,060 --> 00:42:12,830
Jon Snow.

410
00:42:13,610 --> 00:42:15,880
Hush. Don't talk.

411
00:42:20,770 --> 00:42:22,160
Do you remember the cave?

412
00:42:27,810 --> 00:42:29,680
We should have stayed in the cave.

413
00:42:34,210 --> 00:42:35,390
We'll go back there.

414
00:42:42,490 --> 00:42:45,280
You know nothing, Jon Snow.

415
00:43:21,120 --> 00:43:22,880
Drop the scythe, boys!

416
00:43:45,510 --> 00:43:47,580
-Hoist her up.  -Hoist her up!

417
00:43:54,050 --> 00:43:55,600
They've had enough for one night.

418
00:44:00,460 --> 00:44:01,950
Don't cheer too loud.

419
00:44:03,970 --> 00:44:06,270
They still outnumber us 1,000 to one.

420
00:44:15,270 --> 00:44:16,020
Tormund.

421
00:44:17,060 --> 00:44:17,830
It's over.

422
00:44:19,760 --> 00:44:20,570
Let it end.

423
00:44:21,740 --> 00:44:23,000
This is how a man ends.

424
00:44:31,500 --> 00:44:32,370
Put him in chains.

425
00:44:33,730 --> 00:44:34,910
We'll question him later.

426
00:44:38,590 --> 00:44:39,550
I should have thrown you

427
00:44:40,960 --> 00:44:42,810
from the top of the Wall, boy!

428
00:44:44,130 --> 00:44:44,800
Aye.

429
00:44:46,520 --> 00:44:47,260
You should have.

430
00:44:55,470 --> 00:44:57,320
Whoa, it's me. It's me.

431
00:45:01,690 --> 00:45:02,910
I promised you, didn't I?

432
00:45:18,610 --> 00:45:19,500
We held them off.

433
00:45:20,690 --> 00:45:21,430
For one night.

434
00:45:22,300 --> 00:45:23,490
This is a great victory.

435
00:45:25,010 --> 00:45:25,980
A great victory?

436
00:45:28,500 --> 00:45:31,640
Mance was testing our defenses. He almost made it through.

437
00:45:32,640 --> 00:45:34,910
And he has more giants. He has more mammoths.

438
00:45:35,310 --> 00:45:37,200
He has 1,000 times as many men.

439
00:45:41,340 --> 00:45:42,600
They'll hit us again tonight.

440
00:45:44,160 --> 00:45:45,720
Maybe we can hold them off for a day or two,

441
00:45:45,730 --> 00:45:46,980
but we'll never beat them.

442
00:45:49,040 --> 00:45:49,800
Where are we going?

443
00:45:50,530 --> 00:45:51,650
Going to find Mance.

444
00:45:52,500 --> 00:45:54,510
To find, you can't do that.

445
00:45:55,050 --> 00:45:56,450
No one gave you any orders.

446
00:45:58,210 --> 00:45:59,440
Who's left to give orders?

447
00:46:00,860 --> 00:46:03,460
The wildling army's only an army, because of Mance.

448
00:46:04,280 --> 00:46:06,250
He united 100 warring tribes.

449
00:46:06,790 --> 00:46:08,560
Without Mance, they lose their leader.

450
00:46:08,850 --> 00:46:11,160
They lose their purpose. They go back to fighting each other.

451
00:46:11,160 --> 00:46:12,610
Scatter back to their homes.

452
00:46:13,380 --> 00:46:14,270
Without Mance?

453
00:46:15,620 --> 00:46:16,580
You're going to kill him?

454
00:46:16,880 --> 00:46:17,800
I'm gonna try.

455
00:46:17,830 --> 00:46:19,800
They'll never let you within 100 yards of him.

456
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:22,190
And even if they did, even if you managed to kill him.

457
00:46:22,190 --> 00:46:24,630
They'll kill me? If I don't go, they'll kill me anyway.

458
00:46:24,630 --> 00:46:25,950
They'll kill the rest of us, too.

459
00:46:26,330 --> 00:46:27,430
They won't just kill you.

460
00:46:28,850 --> 00:46:30,470
They'll boil you. They'll flay you.

461
00:46:30,480 --> 00:46:31,690
They'll make it last days.

462
00:46:35,090 --> 00:46:37,930
You're right. It's a bad plan.

463
00:46:40,810 --> 00:46:41,690
What's your plan?

464
00:47:26,170 --> 00:47:27,190
They held the gate.

465
00:47:37,610 --> 00:47:39,200
Get some brothers down here to help you.

466
00:47:42,310 --> 00:47:43,600
We need to burn the bodies.

467
00:48:05,470 --> 00:48:06,680
Raise the outer gate.

468
00:48:08,250 --> 00:48:10,070
Then lower it again as soon as I'm out.

469
00:48:22,560 --> 00:48:23,420
What are you doing?

470
00:48:23,890 --> 00:48:25,690
I promised Mormont, I'd never lose it again.

471
00:48:30,660 --> 00:48:31,820
In case I don't come back.

472
00:48:41,050 --> 00:48:41,660
Jon.

473
00:48:47,760 --> 00:48:48,550
Come back.

